   "body": "## 1. Operational Cost Baseline for the Region\n\nThis profile covers Brazil, in the regulator's words: «O Brasil está estruturado para crescer e com projetos concretos na mesa.» It is the federal road and rail infrastructure pipeline as presented by the national land transport regulator, ANTT (Agência Nacional de Transportes Terrestres). For a freight operator the pipeline matters because concession contracts decide where new or rebuilt road and rail capacity is built and by whom; the pages state no toll, tariff or rate effect of that.\n\nThe captured pages hold no operating cost rate for Brazil: no industrial electricity tariff, fuel price, labour rate, port handling charge or haulage rate is stated, so no cost baseline can be given and none is invented. What the regulator does state is a forecast ('previsão') of investment in conceded highways, not in the whole road network. «Hoje, o país conta com mais de 18 mil quilômetros de rodovias concedidas, com previsão de R$ 306 bilhões em investimentos (CAPEX) e R$ 219 bilhões destinados à operação e manutenção (OPEX).» The two components, build-out spending and operation and maintenance spending, are given side by side, so the build-out forecast is the larger of the two (*Analytical inference:* 306 is more than 219). The agency's home page headlines the same federal road portfolio as «Carteira de rodovias federais alcança R$ 525 bilhões entre obras e operação» and says «ANTT regula 35 contratos e 18,1 mil quilômetros» are regulated. *Analytical inference:* 306 plus 219 gives 525, so the headline is consistent with the two components above.\n\n## 2. Feasibility of Specific Operational Choices\n\nNo page in the captured material gives a permit verdict for on-site solar, battery storage, equipment import or in-region sourcing in Brazil, so no verdict of possible, restricted or prohibited is stated here. The only choice the material speaks to is the rail option: «No setor ferroviário, são 15 mil quilômetros operacionais, além de novos projetos estruturantes e ampliações em curso.» «No setor ferroviário, a agenda inclui novos leilões, renovações contratuais e projetos estratégicos, como a Ferrogrão e a EF-118, além da ampliação da malha existente.» *Analytical inference:* resting on these two sentences, rail capacity exists today and is still being extended, so a rail leg is an option the regulator itself describes as growing, but the pages give no rail tariff or transit time to price it against road.\n\n## 3. Cost Comparison Against Alternatives\n\nThe captured material gives no per-tonne or per-kilometre cost for road against rail. What it does give is the scale of what is being contracted out for each. For road, «Entre 2023 e 2025, foram realizados 19 leilões rodoviários, totalizando mais de 7 mil quilômetros concedidos e cerca de R$ 230 bilhões em investimentos.» For rail, «Atualmente, o setor ferroviário soma mais de R$ 227 bilhões em novos aportes, com milhares de quilômetros autorizados e dezenas de contratos vigentes.» The two figures measure different things (road auction investment against new rail investment, one stated as 'cerca de' and the other as 'mais de'), so no ratio is drawn. *Analytical inference:* resting on these two sentences, the pages hold no rate for either mode, so any road versus rail comparison for a Brazilian lane has to rely on rates from carriers.\n\n## 7. Pending Changes That Shift the Calculus\n\nThe agency presented its 2026 agenda in a news item marked «Publicado em 15/04/2026». «Para 2026, estão previstos novos leilões que somam mais de 3.200 quilômetros e R$ 71,6 bilhões.» The completed cycle is stated as 'mais de 7 mil' kilometres and 'cerca de R$ 230 bilhões', and the 2026 round as 'mais de 3.200' kilometres and 'R$ 71,6 bilhões'; these are lower bounds or approximations, so no ratio between the two is drawn. The home page adds that «três leilões de 2026 somam quase R$ 32 bilhões e BR-163/MT/PA será o próximo ativo levado à B3». The rail agenda for the year includes new auctions, contract renewals and the Ferrogrão and EF-118 projects (quoted in section 2). *Analytical inference:* resting on these sentences, the 2026 auction round and the rail agenda are the stages at which road or rail capacity on a corridor may change; no page states a toll or tariff change for any named lane.\n\n- 2023: «Entre 2023 e 2025, foram realizados 19 leilões rodoviários» (completed road auction cycle, 2023 to 2025)\n- 2026: «Para 2026, estão previstos novos leilões que somam mais de 3.200 quilômetros e R$ 71,6 bilhões» (planned road auctions)\n\n## 8. Sources\n\n- ANTT, news item on the ANTT presentation of its investment portfolio at FIESP, published 15/04/2026: https://www.gov.br/antt/pt-br/assuntos/ultimas-noticias/na-fiesp-antt-apresenta-carteira-de-r-300-bilhoes-e-reforca-seguranca-para-investimentos-em-infraestrutura-no-brasil\n- ANTT, home page news headlines: https://www.gov.br/antt/pt-br\n",
